  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a complex but consistent relationship between (-)-Menthyl propionate and SNU1, with the drug acting as a target for multiple downstream molecules. The primary pathway involves (-)-Menthyl propionate directly targeting SNU-387, which in turn is a target of several compounds, including 10,22-Dihydroxy-7,7,18,18-tetramethyl-8,13,17-trioxapentacyclo[12.8.0.03,12.04,9.016,21]docosa-1(22),3(12),4(9),10,14,16(21),19-heptaen-2-one and Gypenoside Xlvi. All of these molecules ultimately target SNU1, indicating a hierarchical pathway where (-)-Menthyl propionate may influence SNU1 through a series of intermediate targets. The evidence supports a mechanism where the drug's activity is mediated through a chain of molecular interactions, with SNU1 being the final endpoint of this cascade. The consistency across different paths and the shared targets suggest a plausible, though not fully elucidated, mechanism of action.",
